+# Runbook: Vault Productionization (Aegis AI platform)
+
+Goal: Deploy Vault in HA with auto‑unseal and enable secure CI OIDC flows.
+
+Pre-reqs:
+- Cloud KMS key (BYOK allowed) or managed KMS access
+- Terraform / Helm access, cluster-admin privileges
+
+Steps:
+1. Provision KMS key (BYOK if customer requires) and record ARN/ID.
+2. Deploy Vault Helm chart with raft storage and auto-unseal (use helm/values-vault-production.yaml). Validate pods in namespace `vault`.
+3. Configure Kubernetes auth and create policy `aegis-ci` with limited capabilities for CI signer role.
+4. Create OIDC role for GitHub Actions and map subject to `aegis-ci` policy.
+5. Create Transit key for signing: `vault write -f transit/keys/aegis-signing-key`
+6. Test end-to-end: GitHub Action OIDC login → request token → vault login → transit sign test.
+7. Configure HA probes, backups of raft snapshot and periodic snapshot restore drills monthly.
+
+Incident play:
+- If Vault unreachable: fail CI signing, enable temporary manual HIL flow for promotions (see HIL runbook).
+- If key compromise suspected: rotate transit key and re-sign artifacts as needed; notify compliance.
+
